DIAGNOSTIC (not for merge): trace drm_gem_dumb_map_offset

DRM_IOCTL_MODE_MAP_DUMB panics on a device-tree DRM device
(nextbsd-kernel#176):

	panic: vm_fault failed: 0xffff0000007d8d00 error 1
	#5 drm_gem_dumb_map_offset+0x2c
	#6 drm_ioctl_kernel -> drm_ioctl

Two things are already established by testing rather than reading:

  MAP_DUMB with a bogus handle returns ENOENT cleanly, so the
  spin_lock(&filp->table_lock) and idr_find() in objects_lookup() are fine.

  DESTROY_DUMB on a real handle works, and it does the same lookup plus a
  reference drop -- so lookup with a real object is fine too.

That leaves drm_gem_create_mmap_offset(), and guessing which pointer inside
it is bad has not converged. This prints the object, its device, the vma
offset manager and the return code so the next run says which one.

Revert before merging.
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/drm_gem.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/drm_gem.c
@@ -371,20 +371,29 @@
 	int ret;
 
 	obj = drm_gem_object_lookup(file, handle);
+	printf("fkms-dbg: map_offset handle=%u obj=%p\n", handle, obj);
 	if (!obj)
 		return -ENOENT;
 
+	printf("fkms-dbg:   obj->dev=%p size=%zu import_attach=%p\n",
+	    obj->dev, (size_t)obj->size, obj->import_attach);
+	printf("fkms-dbg:   vma_offset_manager=%p funcs=%p\n",
+	    obj->dev != NULL ? obj->dev->vma_offset_manager : NULL, obj->funcs);
+
 	/* Don't allow imported objects to be mapped */
 	if (drm_gem_is_imported(obj)) {
 		ret = -EINVAL;
 		goto out;
 	}
 
+	printf("fkms-dbg:   calling drm_gem_create_mmap_offset\n");
 	ret = drm_gem_create_mmap_offset(obj);
+	printf("fkms-dbg:   create_mmap_offset ret=%d\n", ret);
 	if (ret)
 		goto out;
 
 	*offset = drm_vma_node_offset_addr(&obj->vma_node);
+	printf("fkms-dbg:   offset=0x%llx\n", (unsigned long long)*offset);
 out:
 	drm_gem_object_put(obj);
 
